The MyUBAT landing page serves as a vital digital interface, yet relying on direct repository access for static assets creates avoidable latency. As our user base grows, fetching files directly from the origin server introduces bottlenecks that compromise the immediacy of the user experience and overall page performance.

To address this, we are leveraging jsDelivr, a high-performance public CDN, to serve assets directly from our GitHub repository. By utilizing jsDelivr’s robust multi-CDN infrastructure, we effectively distribute our code across a global network of edge servers, ensuring that users retrieve data from the location physically closest to them.

This integration significantly reduces network latency and optimizes Time to First Byte (TTFB). By bridging our GitHub repository with jsDelivr’s delivery network, we ensure near-instantaneous page rendering, providing MyUBAT users with a frictionless and responsive browsing experience that reflects our technical standards.
